{"id":"GEOG661","title":"Fundamentals of Geospatial Intelligence","department":"Geographical Sciences","level":"Grad","credits":"3","description":"Geospatial Intelligence (GEOINT) is the collection, analysis, visualization and dissemination of geospatial information to support decision-making. This course introduces the fundamental knowledge required to become a successful GEOINT practitioner, including the history of the GEOINT discipline, the intelligence applications of remote sensing and Geographic Information Systems (GIS) technologies, and how GEOINT products are used to support national security and humanitarian missions. Upon completion of this course you will understand the roles that technology, policy, doctrine, government, and industry play in shaping the Geospatial Intelligence discipline, and develop the technical knowledge and domain expertise to create basic GEOINT products that provide context for decision makers.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201801","sections":2,"seats":30,"openSeats":25,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Micah Brachman"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":3,"seats":25,"openSeats":6,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Micah Brachman"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":2,"seats":30,"openSeats":9,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Micah Brachman"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":2,"seats":30,"openSeats":28,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Micah Brachman"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":4,"seats":41,"openSeats":22,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Madeleine Guy"],"removed":false},{"term":"202201","sections":4,"seats":80,"openSeats":67,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["David Cook"],"removed":false},{"term":"202208","sections":2,"seats":35,"openSeats":12,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Jonathon Hathaway"],"removed":false},{"term":"202301","sections":2,"seats":40,"openSeats":32,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["David Cook"],"removed":false},{"term":"2023